{"answer":"There are 7 such subsets: {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}, {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}. For example, {1,8} has sum 9. The list is exhaustive: a subset with four or more distinct positive elements has sum at least 1+2+3+4=10; the possible pairs and triples summing to 9 are exactly those listed.","approaches":[{"description":"Enumerate subsets by cardinality, using a minimum-sum bound to eliminate cardinality at least four.","id":"cardinality-enumeration","outcome":"candidate","reason":"It produces a complete finite list and a direct exhaustiveness argument."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived by steps rule-out-four, enumerate-pairs, enumerate-triples, and total-count.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["pair-list","triple-list","large-subsets-impossible"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"count-seven","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Exactly 7 subsets of {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} have sum 9.","step_ids":["total-count"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in enumerate-pairs.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"pair-list","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The two-element subsets summing to 9 are {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, and {4,5}.","step_ids":["enumerate-pairs"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in enumerate-triples.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"triple-list","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The three-element subsets summing to 9 are {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, and {2,3,4}.","step_ids":["enumerate-triples"],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Derived in rule-out-four.","citations":[],"critical":false,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"large-subsets-impossible","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"No subset with four or more elements can have sum 9.","step_ids":["rule-out-four"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":[],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"rule-out-four","justification":"The least possible sum of four distinct positive elements is 1+2+3+4=10. Adding further positive elements only increases the sum.","statement":"A subset summing to 9 has at most three elements."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"enumerate-pairs","justification":"For an ordered pair a<b with a+b=9, a<9/2, so a is 1, 2, 3, or 4. The complementary values are respectively 8, 7, 6, and 5.","statement":"The complete list of two-element subsets summing to 9 is {1,8}, {2,7}, {3,6}, {4,5}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":[],"id":"enumerate-triples","justification":"Write a<b<c. If a=1, then b+c=8 with b<c, giving (b,c)=(2,6),(3,5). If a=2, then b+c=7 and b>2, giving (3,4). If a>=3, then a+b+c>=3+4+5=12, impossible.","statement":"The complete list of three-element subsets summing to 9 is {1,2,6}, {1,3,5}, {2,3,4}."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["rule-out-four","enumerate-pairs","enumerate-triples"],"id":"total-count","justification":"The empty subset has sum 0 and no singleton has sum 9 because every available element is at most 8. Steps enumerate-pairs and enumerate-triples give 4 and 3 subsets, while rule-out-four excludes all remaining cardinalities.","statement":"The total number is 4+3=7."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
